# What fzf-caffeinate.sh needs, declared beside it.
# Format is name | kind | locator | policy | reason, and the collector stamps the consumer.
# The system kind because this one ships with macOS at a fixed absolute path rather than
# arriving through a package manager.
caffeinate | system | /usr/bin/caffeinate | required | holding the machine awake, the whole point of that picker
# Backgrounding the caffeinate process so it outlives this popup. system for the same reason as
# the line above, it ships with macOS at a fixed absolute path. Required rather than optional
# because there is no fallback path here, without it the hold is tied to a popup that closes.
nohup | system | /usr/bin/nohup | required | detaching caffeinate so the hold survives the popup that started it
